## Topics Already Covered (banter only)

These are the explicit banter topics this party has already used. **Do not pick a topic that is the same theme as any of these — even loosely related counts as repetition.** "Complaining about the cold" and "remarking on the weather" are the same theme; "ribbing about a missed arrow" and "ribbing about clumsy footwork" are the same theme.

{# day / gameDay: whole game days, from a DLL and script that send them; older entries carry none. #}
{% set recent = default(recentBanter, []) %}
{% set today = default(gameDay, -1) %}
{% if length(recent) > 0 %}
{% for r in recent %}
- {% if today >= 0 and existsIn(r, "day") %}[{% if r.day >= today %}today{% else if r.day == today - 1 %}yesterday{% else %}{{ today - r.day }} days ago{% endif %}] {% endif %}{{ r.speaker }} & {{ r.target }}: "{{ r.topic }}"
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No prior banter topics on record. Wide-open field.
{% endif %}

## Rotation Pressure — recent speakers and recent pairs

Banter goes stale fastest when the same pair trades lines every time with the same one opening. Use the lists below to rotate away from whoever just spoke.

{% set lastSpeakers = [] %}
{% set lastPairs = [] %}
{% for r in recent %}
{% if r.speaker != "" and r.target != "" %}
{% set lastSpeakers = append(lastSpeakers, r.speaker) %}
{% set lastPairs = append(lastPairs, r.speaker + " & " + r.target) %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if length(lastSpeakers) > 0 %}
**Recent speakers (most recent at the bottom):**
{% for s in lastSpeakers %}
- {{ s }}
{% endfor %}

**Recent banter pairs (most recent at the bottom):**
{% for p in lastPairs %}
- {{ p }}
{% endfor %}

**Hard rotation rule (read this carefully):**
1. Look at the LAST entry in "Recent speakers" — that follower CANNOT be the speaker this turn. Pick a different speaker (swap roles within the pair if needed), and favor whoever has opened least lately.
{% if followerCount >= 3 %}
2. Look at the LAST entry in "Recent banter pairs" — that exact pair (in either order) CANNOT banter this turn. Pick a different pair, even if it means lower affinity.
3. If no pair is left after these filters, output {"banter":null}. Silence is better than repetition.
{% else %}
2. With only two companions here, this pair is the only option: vary who opens and what about.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
No recent banters on record — any pair is fair game. Pick the most thematically interesting pair, not just the highest-affinity one.
{% endif %}

